# Non-Dict Record polymorphic scheme preservation at document boundaries.
# Doc 1: make-record returns a record with a polymorphic identity function.
#         The dict result is passed via % to Doc 2.
# Doc 2: %.make-record is accessed via %, called to produce the record.
#         This non-Dict expression at the document boundary tests that
#         typecheck_document increments level before inference and generalizes
#         the Record fields as polymorphic schemes (Fix #3, Cycle #31).
# Doc 3: %.id accesses the identity function from the previous document's result.
[make-record: [fn [] [id: [fn [x] x]]]]
---
[call %.make-record]
---
[result: [call %.id 42]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Int(42)})
